WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.700
So let's start actually getting our sequence set up

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:08.150
and adding our actors to our sequence.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.689
So to keep consistency, we're going

4
00:00:09.689 --> 00:00:13.429
to create a new folder called SEQ underscore EX for example.

5
00:00:13.429 --> 00:00:16.070
So we'll create that, and then we'll create a new level

6
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.250
sequence as well.

7
00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.070
So jump back to our project, and I'm

8
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.030
going to go ahead and just delete our classroom

9
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.429
folder and the level sequence, which is totally fine.

10
00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:26.910
Go back to my sequence 105, and I'm

11
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.910
going to right click under here, do new folder,

12
00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.390
and we'll call this SEQ underscore EX for example.

13
00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:35.130
We'll double click to go into this folder,

14
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.630
and again, we can create a new level sequence

15
00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.909
by clicking the little dropdown here and add level sequence.

16
00:00:40.909 --> 00:00:42.869
Let me go ahead and delete this one from there.

17
00:00:42.869 --> 00:00:45.469
Or we can also do it through our content browser,

18
00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:47.429
but because we do want this in our scene,

19
00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:49.789
let's go ahead and just do add level sequence.

20
00:00:49.789 --> 00:00:50.710
And we jump back.

21
00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:56.149
We're going to name this to SEQ underscore 105 EX for example.

22
00:00:56.149 --> 00:00:58.609
So go into our example folder, and we'll

23
00:00:58.609 --> 00:01:03.450
call this SEQ underscore 105 EX for example, click Save.

24
00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.890
And because we use that dropdown,

25
00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.290
it will automatically place it into our world.

26
00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:10.209
So I'm going to fly into here real quick,

27
00:01:10.209 --> 00:01:12.769
and let's just move it kind of in the center

28
00:01:12.769 --> 00:01:15.010
of our little stage here, just

29
00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:16.870
so we know that this is where the action is

30
00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.250
going to be occurring in case we need to open this quickly.

31
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.569
And you see as well that it went ahead and just

32
00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:25.010
automatically opened our sequence

33
00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:26.890
with the sequence active.

34
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:29.489
If at any point you close your sequence, don't worry.

35
00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.489
That's totally fine.

36
00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:32.890
A couple of ways we can do this, we can click

37
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.209
the actual icon in the world.

38
00:01:35.209 --> 00:01:37.090
So we can see here, sequence 105 EX

39
00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.930
and click open level sequence.

40
00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.930
Or we can go back to our content browser

41
00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.650
underneath here and just double click it,

42
00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:45.049
and we'll open up our sequence.

43
00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:46.609
All right, perfect.

44
00:01:46.609 --> 00:01:48.849
So the first step that we want to do after creating

45
00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:51.510
our sequence is start staging some of our actors.

46
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.650
Now if you recall, we can do spawnables.

47
00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:56.900
We can access content that's already in the level.

48
00:01:56.939 --> 00:01:59.659
But for the purposes of what we're building here,

49
00:01:59.659 --> 00:02:02.700
we're actually going to drag the actors into the world

50
00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.060
first, and then we're going to add them to our sequence.

51
00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.540
And the reason for that is if I jump over,

52
00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.500
eventually our whole shot will kind of

53
00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.620
culminate to this little point here in the map.

54
00:02:11.620 --> 00:02:15.259
But we want to start way in the building in the back.

55
00:02:15.259 --> 00:02:19.500
So if I were just to simply drag the little bot

56
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.099
character into the sequence, it would place it

57
00:02:22.099 --> 00:02:24.340
at 0, 0, 0 on our origin, which

58
00:02:24.340 --> 00:02:27.030
is not really what I want.

59
00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.909
So I'm going to go to my content browser.

60
00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:30.870
Now in this case, it's going to be a little difficult

61
00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.629
to try to drag back and forth.

62
00:02:32.629 --> 00:02:36.819
So I'm just going to dock this in my layout.

63
00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:37.379
There we go.

64
00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:38.780
So we've got this, and I'm going

65
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.819
to drag it off and move it to the side here.

66
00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:43.930
Perfect.

67
00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.930
OK, so what we're going to look for actually

68
00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:47.810
is this little SKM bot.

69
00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:50.050
You'll see it's in the characters bot mesh.

70
00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.889
I'll show you a little shortcut here,

71
00:02:51.889 --> 00:02:55.240
where we're just going to search for SKM underscore bot

72
00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:57.240
by clicking our root content folder,

73
00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.560
and I'm going to do SKM underscore.

74
00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:00.599
You'll see bot.

75
00:03:00.599 --> 00:03:04.039
And what I'm going to do is drag him into our level here.

76
00:03:04.039 --> 00:03:05.800
Now just to show you real quick,

77
00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.879
go ahead and keep yours in the level itself.

78
00:03:07.879 --> 00:03:10.039
But if I delete this and drag it into our sequence,

79
00:03:10.039 --> 00:03:12.759
you'll see that it in fact does put it at our 0, 0

80
00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.159
location, even though it is in our sequence, which

81
00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:17.080
is not what we want.

82
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.020
So we're going to drag him back up to our stage here.

83
00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.419
Now what we want to do is actually add this actor

84
00:03:22.419 --> 00:03:23.419
to our sequence.

85
00:03:23.419 --> 00:03:26.500
And that's very easy to do is inside of our sequence,

86
00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.860
we can simply right click, Add Actor to Sequence.

87
00:03:29.860 --> 00:03:33.060
So I'll have my SKM bot selected.

88
00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.340
And inside of my sequence in the content section

89
00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:39.460
here on the left, right click, Add Actor to Sequence.

90
00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.340
Now you will notice that we have

91
00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.969
all of the content within our actual level present here.

92
00:03:45.969 --> 00:03:47.129
We could even do a search.

93
00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:47.889
I could do SKM.

94
00:03:47.889 --> 00:03:49.409
There's the SKM bot.

95
00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:53.009
Or you'll see because we have the asset selected inside

96
00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:55.569
of the level already, it's the first thing

97
00:03:55.569 --> 00:03:56.449
that's available here.

98
00:03:56.849 --> 00:03:58.210
So I'll just go ahead and click this.

99
00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:00.129
And you'll see now it's added to our sequence.

100
00:04:00.129 --> 00:04:02.849
And now we can start manipulating it and changing it

101
00:04:02.849 --> 00:04:03.889
as we need.

102
00:04:03.889 --> 00:04:06.129
The next thing you want to do is actually

103
00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:08.090
convert this to a spawnable.

104
00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.610
With the character in the world right now,

105
00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:11.490
he actually exists.

106
00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:12.969
So even if I closed my sequence,

107
00:04:12.969 --> 00:04:15.250
so I'm going to just save this and close my sequence,

108
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.930
you'll see that the bot stays within the world, which

109
00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:20.610
is not what we want because players would see this.

110
00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.769
They could interact with it.

111
00:04:21.769 --> 00:04:24.889
They could run into it, which is not really what we want.

112
00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:28.810
We just want this actor present inside of the sequence itself.

113
00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:30.649
So again, I could go back up to,

114
00:04:30.649 --> 00:04:32.410
I could find my sequence in the world here.

115
00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:37.009
Or I could simply just drop down sequence 105X, open it,

116
00:04:37.009 --> 00:04:38.449
and now we have our bot.

117
00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:40.009
So I'm going to right click on it.

118
00:04:40.009 --> 00:04:42.209
And what I want to do is convert to spawnable.

119
00:04:42.209 --> 00:04:43.569
So as soon as I do that, you'll

120
00:04:43.569 --> 00:04:45.209
see that it changes to a lightning bolt.

121
00:04:45.209 --> 00:04:48.009
We can confirm that in our outliner.

122
00:04:48.009 --> 00:04:49.009
Save my sequence.

123
00:04:49.009 --> 00:04:50.589
And if I close the sequence, you'll

124
00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:52.250
see that the character disappears.

125
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.370
Again, one of the advantages of using

126
00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.730
our spawnables versus possessables.

127
00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:00.050
So he only exists as long as this sequence is open.

128
00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:02.430
Now that our actor is present inside of our sequence,

129
00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.850
we want to go ahead and add some animation to it.

130
00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:07.610
So to do that, we're going to click the asset itself

131
00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.050
and add an animation.

132
00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:11.930
Now, the first one that we want to add is this run.

133
00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.740
So from the final sequence that we'll have,

134
00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:18.540
we want the character to run to the end of the platform,

135
00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.860
jump, and then free fall.

136
00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.779
So we're going to use three separate animations.

137
00:05:21.819 --> 00:05:23.939
The first one's starting with the run.

138
00:05:23.939 --> 00:05:25.779
So I'm going to go ahead and take the character.

139
00:05:25.779 --> 00:05:27.819
And with my rotation snapping on, I'm

140
00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:30.060
going to rotate him 90 degrees

141
00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:33.439
so he's facing the end of the platform.

142
00:05:33.439 --> 00:05:34.860
So I'm going to select the asset.

143
00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.519
I can also select it from the sequence.

144
00:05:36.519 --> 00:05:38.019
And you'll see animation here.

145
00:05:38.019 --> 00:05:41.579
I'm going to keep my play head at 0, 0, 0, which

146
00:05:41.579 --> 00:05:43.579
if you want a quick snap, we can actually just

147
00:05:43.579 --> 00:05:47.480
do this to front, to the front of the sequence.

148
00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.259
Click my animation, a little plus,

149
00:05:49.259 --> 00:05:51.579
and I'm going to look for run.

150
00:05:51.579 --> 00:05:53.500
We should see a bot run.

151
00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:55.699
So go ahead and add this to the animation.

152
00:05:55.699 --> 00:05:58.079
You see that the character already has some movement.

153
00:05:58.079 --> 00:05:59.040
Let's go and do this.

154
00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.500
And if I play the sequence, you'll

155
00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:04.019
see he plays the animation once, and that's it.

156
00:06:04.019 --> 00:06:05.819
So the next thing that we want to do

157
00:06:05.819 --> 00:06:06.980
is actually extend this out.

158
00:06:06.980 --> 00:06:08.639
Now, in this case, let's extend it out

159
00:06:08.639 --> 00:06:09.579
to about 150 frames.

160
00:06:09.579 --> 00:06:11.379
We may adjust this later.

161
00:06:11.379 --> 00:06:14.100
So I'm going to highlight over my animation, which

162
00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:20.779
is this a bot run, and click and drag the end here to 150.

163
00:06:20.819 --> 00:06:23.620
And you see now, if I scrub this back and hit play,

164
00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.019
you see that he actually plays his animation,

165
00:06:26.019 --> 00:06:28.579
continues to cycle over.

166
00:06:28.579 --> 00:06:30.160
So now what we want to do is actually

167
00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.139
add some key frames to make it look like the character is

168
00:06:33.139 --> 00:06:33.959
actually running.

169
00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:36.379
So we're going to set one key frame at the start,

170
00:06:36.379 --> 00:06:39.360
and we're going to key our location, rotation, and scale.

171
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.639
And we're going to use our key frame to change.

172
00:06:42.639 --> 00:06:44.279
So if any of those properties change,

173
00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:46.560
to automatically key frame as well.

174
00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:50.410
Or we could just simply add a key frame manually.

175
00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.449
All right, so let's jump back over to our sequence.

176
00:06:52.449 --> 00:06:54.610
So I'm going to roughly put the character.

177
00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:58.290
Now, he is slightly off, so I'm going to rotate him about,

178
00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.490
do 10 degrees.

179
00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:03.769
So now he's lined up with the end here, select the SKM bot.

180
00:07:03.769 --> 00:07:06.170
I'm going to expand out my transforms here,

181
00:07:06.170 --> 00:07:08.689
and click this little plus button to add a key frame.

182
00:07:08.689 --> 00:07:12.490
Now, it's important, wherever your time slider is located

183
00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:14.329
is where it's going to add those key frames.

184
00:07:14.329 --> 00:07:17.610
So let's say that I add key frames at 61 frames.

185
00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:18.290
Not a problem.

186
00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:22.529
I can just select them all and drag them back to zero.

187
00:07:22.529 --> 00:07:24.370
All right, so this is our starting position.

188
00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:28.029
And let's go ahead and move forward about 90 frames.

189
00:07:28.029 --> 00:07:31.230
And then if you have this create key frame automatically

190
00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:34.949
turned on, if I then press W to go into move.

191
00:07:34.949 --> 00:07:37.189
And if I move my character, you'll

192
00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:39.389
notice that we get something interesting here.

193
00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:42.490
So we get a point, which is the start of our key.

194
00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:45.750
And this is the end where we created this new key.

195
00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.629
So if I didn't have auto key frame turned on,

196
00:07:48.629 --> 00:07:51.069
it wouldn't automatically create this key.

197
00:07:51.069 --> 00:07:52.870
So make sure that if you don't, go ahead

198
00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:54.529
and click the little plus button again

199
00:07:54.529 --> 00:07:55.509
to create your keys.

200
00:07:55.509 --> 00:07:57.069
Now, an important note here, you'll

201
00:07:57.069 --> 00:07:59.269
notice that our location, rotation, and scale all

202
00:07:59.269 --> 00:08:00.269
have keys.

203
00:08:00.269 --> 00:08:02.569
However, location only has a new key.

204
00:08:02.569 --> 00:08:05.509
And that's because the only location that really changed

205
00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:06.990
was my x and y.

206
00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.389
The character never went vertically.

207
00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:10.589
He just went x and y.

208
00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:12.709
Hence why we only have these two additional keys.

209
00:08:12.709 --> 00:08:14.069
So just to keep that in mind.

210
00:08:14.069 --> 00:08:15.750
So if we go back to the beginning here

211
00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:17.110
and we play our animation, you'll

212
00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:20.189
see that he kind of starts to ramp up and out.

213
00:08:20.189 --> 00:08:22.870
And then he stops, which is what we want.

214
00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:24.550
Now, if you notice, there's something

215
00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:26.629
a little weird about this opening animation

216
00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:30.269
that he kind of starts to run, get some velocity,

217
00:08:30.269 --> 00:08:32.470
and then he's up to speed, which is not really

218
00:08:32.470 --> 00:08:33.110
what we want.

219
00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.870
We want him hitting the ground running.

220
00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.370
So to do that, we're actually going

221
00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.029
to change our key frames, these first ones.

222
00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:41.230
So I'm going to click drag over these.

223
00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:43.299
And then right click, I'm going

224
00:08:43.299 --> 00:08:45.460
to change the key interpolation to linear.

225
00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.460
So I'll come back to this in a second and explain.

226
00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.580
But now if we go back to the front and press play,

227
00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.460
you see that he's already running.

228
00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.840
And that doesn't look too bad.

229
00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.320
Now, something else to note here

230
00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:56.759
is that because of our key frames,

231
00:08:56.759 --> 00:08:59.639
you'll see that he starts to slow down towards the end.

232
00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:01.080
So we'll do the same thing.

233
00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.279
We will select this key frame, right click,

234
00:09:03.279 --> 00:09:04.639
and change it to linear.

235
00:09:04.639 --> 00:09:06.960
And so now, if we play back the animation,

236
00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:10.360
looks like he's running right to the end, which is perfect.

237
00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.669
That's exactly what we need.

238
00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:15.429
So the next step here is to go ahead and add

239
00:09:15.429 --> 00:09:16.830
two additional animations.

240
00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:19.549
So we're going to add the jump and then the fall.

241
00:09:19.549 --> 00:09:20.990
So we'll do that really quickly.

242
00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:22.990
And then we'll work on our key frame.

243
00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:26.090
So I'm going to go back to here.

244
00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:28.669
And what I'm going to do is let's take our A bot run.

245
00:09:28.669 --> 00:09:31.929
And we know that from this movement, he runs to the end.

246
00:09:31.929 --> 00:09:35.289
And at this key frame, we want him to jump.

247
00:09:35.289 --> 00:09:36.809
So I'm going to take this handle,

248
00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:39.850
drag it back right to our key frame.

249
00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.970
And then I'm going to go ahead and click animation.

250
00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:44.610
Let's expand this out.

251
00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.529
I'm going to add another animation.

252
00:09:46.529 --> 00:09:48.210
And in this case, we are looking

253
00:09:48.210 --> 00:09:51.610
for jump, which is a bot run jump.

254
00:09:51.610 --> 00:09:53.730
And you'll see that it adds, if I move this off,

255
00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.330
you'll see it adds a secondary animation to our set.

256
00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:59.009
So go ahead and undo that real quick.

